    "description": "STRATOS is a direct-air-capture project being developed in Ector County, Texas. The facility is intended to remove carbon dioxide directly from the atmosphere and serve carbon-management and sequestration markets rather than conventional power demand. Its operating model is asset-heavy and project-based because value depends on a large-scale carbon-removal facility, associated sequestration infrastructure, and contracted carbon-management demand. 1PointFive's public materials state that the project is designed to capture up to 500,000 tonnes of carbon dioxide per year. Operations are concentrated in Texas as a single flagship carbon-removal facility. Occidental and BlackRock announced a joint venture for the project in 2023, but public sources do not disclose the final ownership percentages between 1PointFive and BlackRock clients.",
